<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20876] efalnd: Fix double free of QP/CQ on device init failure</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20876</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The QP/CQ cleanup helper frees the queue pair array and the manager&lt;br/&gt;
queue pair but leaves the stored pointers dangling. On a device&lt;br/&gt;
initialization failure the cleanup runs once during the creation&lt;br/&gt;
helper's own error handling and then a second time from the device&lt;br/&gt;
teardown path, which only checks the pointers for NULL. The dangling&lt;br/&gt;
pointers pass that check, so the second pass iterates already freed&lt;br/&gt;
memory and frees it again, causing a use-after-free and double free.&lt;br/&gt;
In addition, the completion queue create error path returns the is-error predicate&lt;br/&gt;
instead of the actual negative error code.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment />
